## 3. Industry-Specific Risk
**Part A — Why This Company Can Compound:**  
Semiconductor demand → KLAC’s inspection tools → yield improvements for customers → increased fab utilization → higher demand for KLAC’s tools.  

This self-reinforcing loop ensures recurring revenue and margin expansion, solidifying KLAC’s market position.  

**Durability Verdict:** Strong — KLAC’s value chain is resilient to industry cycles.  

**Part B — Capex Cycle Risk:**  
KLAC is highly dependent on foundries (fab-heavy model) with significant exposure to data center and consumer end-markets. Its customer concentration in TSMC, Samsung, and Micron increases vulnerability during inventory digestion phases.  

**Severity:** **MEDIUM** — High dependency on a few customers and cyclical end-markets.

